      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2016 Elsevier Masson SAS. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "Obesity is a frequent disease, due to complex causes. Importantly, its related medical and psychosocial comorbidities are linked to its severity. Thus, the first thorough evaluation is mandatory in order to build a personalized care program, which needs to be in agreement with all the health professionals involved. This care program also needs to be reevaluated and possibly modified during the follow-up. The care objectives need to be realistic and in agreement with what the patients is expecting."
      },
